  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to Ebola Epidemic in Sierra Leone through Social Mobilization in Kailahun and Kenema Dist</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contain the spread of the virus in the nine affected and districts at risk effective community mobilisation on understanding the disease and preventive measures is fundamental. Therefore CAFOD with other Catholic Development Agencies provided funds to National Caritas of Sierra Leone to complement the efforts of government to contain the spread of the disease in the affected districts of Kailahun and Kenema, and districts at risk (Kono) by scaling up effective community-based awareness raising. The project intervention logic include 1) selection of 100 community advocate (CA) from the Catholic Parishes in the affected area and training them for two day on prevention measure of EVD, 2) work closely with Ministry of Health and Sanitation, UNICEF, MSF and WHO to review and update current IEC material on Ebola, and 3) conducting 10 consecutive sensitizations during Sunday masses.</narrative>
  </description>
